From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 18:35:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cam: isp: raise CAM_ISP_CTX_REQ_MAX to 20 for camerad queue
 depth

camerad keeps VIPC_BUFFER_COUNT (18) requests in flight; the ISP ctx
request pool was 8, so the 10th CONFIG_DEV returned ENOMEM. Raise to 20
(the generic CAM_CTX_REQ_MAX is already 20).
---
 .../msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h      | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h
index f885920..dc97523 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/cam_isp_context.h
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 #define CAM_ISP_CTX_RES_MAX                     24
 
 /* max requests per ctx for isp */
-#define CAM_ISP_CTX_REQ_MAX                     8
+#define CAM_ISP_CTX_REQ_MAX                     20
 
 /*
  * Maximum entries in state monitoring array for error logging
